# bitmaps1 — daily active users with bitmaps
#
# Learn: a string is also an array of bits. SETBIT key offset value sets
# bit number offset (here: the user id) to 0 or 1; BITCOUNT counts the
# 1 bits; BITOP AND|OR|XOR|NOT dest key... combines bitmaps. One bit per
# user: a million users per day is 125 KB.
#
# Task: users 5 and 9 were active on 2026-09-29. Record that, then store
# the users active on BOTH 2026-09-28 and 2026-09-29 in active:both and
# print how many there are.
#

SETBIT active:2026-09-29 1 5
SETBIT active:2026-09-29 1 9
BITOP OR active:both active:2026-09-28 active:2026-09-29
BITCOUNT active:both
